  <div class="container">
    <div class="mainTitle_agreements_Submit">
      <h1>Community Guidelines</h1>
      <p>Welcome to BoardGameHive.ro!</p>
      <p>BoardGameHive.ro is where board game enthusiasts gather to play the games 
        they like with more people. It starts the desire for playing 
        board games with other people, and the game you like. 
        By meeting with the others, you might find even more exiting different 
        games in their collection, which you might decide together if you all are interested in 
        playing them. Vote the board games you wish to play, set a time, and a safe place where 
        you can play, and gather around for a fun gathering of board games. All (adults) are welcome to the hive.
      </p>
      <p>
        We want BoardGameHive.ro to be a fun, safe and inclusive space where anyone can be themselves while playing board games and getting to know others. 
        <strong>That’s what these Community Guidelines are for–to set expectations for everyone’s behavior, both on and off of the website.</strong>
        So read on; not following these guidelines can have real consequences-from a nudge to a ban.
      </p>

      <div class="allTheRules">
        <!-- generator - for each   -->
        <!-- template with title and content  -->
        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>BoardGameHive.ro's Rules:</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>1. Consider boundaries. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Comfort levels vary person to person. That’s why we encourage you to Honor, 
                Feedback or even Report a person, so that the others will understand the person better. </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>2. Share cautiously and thoughtfully. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Don’t publicly broadcast your personal information or ways for people to connect 
                with you (no public displays of things like phone numbers, emails, or social handles). 
                Sharing out your bank account numbers or email password is always a bad idea. 
                Don’t ask others to send you their personal details either. 
                Be cautious when sending money to other people. Or maybe don’t at all.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>3. Steer clear of violent content. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We promote positivity and won’t tolerate any sort of violent content that contains gore, 
                death, images or descriptions of violent acts 
                (against humans or animals), use of weapons, and anything advocating or glorifying self-harm.</p>
                <p>If we believe there’s a risk of imminent harm, we may take steps to assist, 
                  like reaching out directly with crisis resources.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>xxx</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>xxx</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>4. Make personal connections, not biz ones. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Don’t advertise, promote, share your social handles to gain followers, sell stuff, fundraise, or campaign.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>5. Just be you. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>People want to meet the real you. Not your fake persona. People are joining to play board game rather than paying attention to others perfections or imperfections.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>6. Communicate Respectfully. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Talking to new people can be tricky, especially when you’re interacting with humans from all walks of life. Respect goes a long way and both ways.</p>
              <p>If the convo goes unexpectedly awry and you find yourself getting upset 
                or feeling angry–pause and reflect before you react. Harassment, threats, 
                bullying, intimidation, doxing, sextortion, blackmail, or anything intentionally 
                done to cause harm is not allowed.</p>
                <p>BoardGameHive.ro is not a place for hate. We will never stand behind racism, bigotry, 
                  hatred, or violence based on who someone is, how they identify or what they look like, 
                  but we believe that people can make mistakes and can grow into avoiding to make them in the future. 
                  This includes (but not limited to) someone’s race, ethnicity, religious affiliation, disability, 
                  physicality, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, or sexual orientation. If you see 
                  someone who doesn't meet your personal criteria, don't invite them, keep them in your invite or write them and move on. 
                  Don't report them unless you think they've violated our policies.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>7. Lead with kindness, not harm.</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Any acts or behavior that suggests, intends, or causes harm to another 
                member - either on or offline, physically or digitally - will be taken very seriously. 
                This includes anything calling for or inciting harm.</p>
                <p>If you have been hurt by someone on BoardGameHive.ro: first, please take care of yourself, 
                  and second, take some time to decide what you need to heal, whether that be 
                  accountability measures, disclosure, support, or all of the above. If this includes 
                  reporting the harm to us, please reach out. We are here for you.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>8. Adults only. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>You must be 18 years of age or older to use BoardGameHive.ro. 
                This also means we don’t allow photos of unaccompanied or 
                unclothed minors, including photos of your younger self–no matter how adorable you were back then.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>9. Abide by the law. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>No illegal content or activities are allowed, ever. This means you can’t use BoardGameHive.ro to break 
                the law, regardless of what it is, such as (but not all): 
                to buy or sell drugs or counterfeit goods, to steal or ask for assistance 
                to help you break the law. We definitely won’t tolerate anyone using BoardGameHive.ro to 
                advocate or participate in any sort of harm involving minors or human trafficking.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>10. One account per person. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Each account can only have one owner. For logistic, privacy and safety 
                reasons, we can’t support multiple people accessing the same account. 
                Each individual needs to have their own.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>11. This is your space, so create and organize the invites you desire. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>Don’t tolerate uncertainty in your invites, remove the players you don’t 
                trust even for a moment or the player who you think might affect the other 
                participants from the invite. If you join an invite, you can leave the invite at 
                any time (no matter the reason), by removing yourself from it. You don’t have to 
                stay in an invite, if you don’t feel to want that. Don’t let the others to influence you. 
                Trust your decisions and keep yourself safe mentally and physically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>12. Be an honest member of the BoardGameHive.ro community. </h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>BoardGameHive.ro. Don’t use BoardGameHive.ro to spread false or misleading info. 
                Don’t spam harmful links or unsolicited content. Don’t create mass accounts. 
                Don’t use BoardGameHive.ro to steal, manipulate, con, or get people to send you money or anything else. 
                Don’t submit misleading reports. 
                Don’t use third-party apps to unlock features or game the system.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="condition_title">
              <h3>13. Stick around to stay active</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>If you don’t log into your BoardGameHive.ro account in less 6 month (up to 1 year), 
                we’ll assume it’s zzZZzzZ and may delete it for inactivity. 
                So if you want to be seen active, just log in from time to time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Reporting</h2>
          </div>
          <div>

            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>As a member of the BoardGameHive.ro community, we encourage you to speak up and speak out. 
                If someone is causing you harm, making you feel uncomfortable, or is violating our Community Guidelines–report it. 
                Your report is always confidential. By reporting, you can help us stop harmful behavior and protect others.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
        </div>



        <div class="category">
          <div class="stretch_title">
            <h2>Impact</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="condition_content">
              <p>We take our Community Guidelines and the impact they have on our community seriously. 
                We’ll do everything we can to make sure people follow them. We have a warning system in place, 
                but if violations continue or if the violation is severe, we will respond accordingly.</p>
              <p>We reserve the right to investigate and/or terminate accounts without a refund of 
                any purchases that might have been done if we find you have misused the Service or behaved 
                in a way BoardGameHive.ro deems inappropriate, unlawful, or in violation of our Community Guidelines 
                or <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Use</a>, including actions or communications that occur off the Service but involve 
                others you meet through the Service.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>









        

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
